## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of practical queue augmentations and min-tracking with guaranteed O(1) per operation.

## Key Concepts
- Min-tracking with stack-based queues
- Amortized analysis of transfers between stacks
- Edge-case handling for empty states and duplicates

## Code Example
```javascript
class MinQueue {
  constructor(){ this.inbox = []; this.outbox = [] }
  _push(stack, val){ const m = stack.length ? Math.min(val, stack[stack.length - 1].min) : val; stack.push({ val, min: m }) }
  enqueue(x){ this._push(this.inbox, x) }
  dequeue(){ if (!this.outbox.length){ while (this.inbox.length){ const el = this.inbox.pop(); const m = this.outbox.length ? Math.min(el.val, this.outbox[this.outbox.length - 1].min) : el.val; this.outbox.push({ val: el.val, min: m }) } }
    return this.outbox.pop().val }
  getMin(){ const mins = []; if (this.inbox.length) mins.push(this.inbox[this.inbox.length - 1].min); if (this.outbox.length) mins.push(this.outbox[this.outbox.length - 1].min); return mins.length ? Math.min(...mins) : undefined }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates ability to implement streaming statistics with efficient data structures and real-time median calculation.

## Key Concepts

- Dual heap structure (max-heap + min-heap)
- Balance invariant maintenance
- Median computation in O(log n) per insert
- Streaming data processing

## Code Example

```javascript
class MedianStream {
  constructor() {
    this.low = new MaxHeap();  // Lower half
    this.high = new MinHeap(); // Upper half
  }

  insert(x) {
    // Insert into appropriate heap and rebalance
    if (this.low.isEmpty() || x <= this.low.peek()) {
      this.low.push(x);
    } else {
      this.high.push(x);
    }

    // Rebalance to maintain size difference ≤ 1
    if (this.low.size() > this.high.size() + 1) {
      this.high.push(this.low.pop());
    } else if (this.high.size() > this.low.size() + 1) {
      this.low.push(this.high.pop());
    }
  }

  getMedian() {
    if (this.low.size() > this.high.size()) {
      return this.low.peek();
    } else if (this.high.size() > this.low.size()) {
      return this.high.peek();
    } else {
      return (this.low.peek() + this.high.peek()) / 2;
    }
  }
}
```

## Implementation Notes

- Duplicates are handled naturally by heap properties
- Memory usage is O(n) for storing all elements
- Suitable for real-time streaming applications
- Can be extended to support removal operations with additional bookkeeping

